@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix gufo: <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

gmeow:ActionPolicy
    a logic:Category ,
        logic:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    rdfs:label "Action Policy"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The action theory governing an agent's whole tool surface: one action schema per advertised tool, each carrying the preconditions that must obtain before the tool may run, the effects that obtain after it does, and — for a write — the compensation that undoes it. It is what makes a tool surface REASONED-ABOUT rather than merely listed: a caller can decide whether an action is admissible without invoking it, and an executed turn can be audited against the theory it claimed to follow."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "The engine's own policy, published as the gmeow://ontology/action-policy resource and the action_policy tool: one schema per advertised tool, tied to it by logic:mcpToolName."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: the THEORY of a tool surface, not a record of what was run. A performed call is a gmeow:ToolCall; the schema that call instantiates belongs here."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid using it for a single tool's schema — that is one member of the policy, not the policy — and avoid it for an access-control rule, which decides who may call rather than what calling means."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Publish one policy per agent surface and tie each schema to its tool by logic:mcpToolName, so the advertised surface and the reasoned-about surface cannot drift apart."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when an agent surface must be reasoned about before it is invoked: checking a precondition, planning a compensation, or auditing an executed turn against the theory it declared."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:ToolCall
    a logic:Event ,
        logic:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    rdfs:label "Tool Call"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Activity ;
    logic:subClassOf
        [
            a logic:Restriction ;
            logic:onProperty gmeow:usedTool ;
            logic:someValuesFrom gmeow:SoftwareAgent ;
        ] ,
        [
            a logic:Restriction ;
            logic:onProperty gmeow:calledByInvocation ;
            logic:allValuesFrom gmeow:ModelInvocation ;
        ] ,
        [
            a logic:Restriction ;
            logic:onProperty gmeow:toolArguments ;
            logic:allValuesFrom rdfs:Literal ;
        ] ,
        [
            a logic:Restriction ;
            logic:onProperty gmeow:toolResult ;
            logic:allValuesFrom rdfs:Literal ;
        ] ;
    skos:definition "One invocation of a tool by an agent: the tool agent (gmeow:usedTool), the requesting model invocation when known (gmeow:calledByInvocation), and the verbatim arguments/result payloads. The agent's actions join the same provenance graph as its claims — an entity the call produced links back via gmeow:wasGeneratedBy (no forward output property, Principle 5), so 'which tool, called by which invocation, with what arguments?' is answerable after the fact. The ModelInvocation idiom one level down."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "An assistant's MCP store_claim call: the ToolCall records the tool agent, the verbatim JSON arguments, and the stored claim's id as the result payload; the claim itself links back with gmeow:wasGeneratedBy."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox .

gmeow:calledByInvocation
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:ToolCall ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    rdfs:label "called by invocation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:ModelInvocation ;
    skos:definition "The model invocation that requested this tool call. Functional: one requesting invocation per call. Optional: a recording harness may not expose the invocation — a ToolCall without one is still auditable provenance."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:derivedBy
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    rdfs:label "derived by"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:ToolCall ;
    skos:definition "The tool call a RESULT STATEMENT came out of — the predicate an annotated result triple carries so an agent's answer stays attributable to the call that produced it. Backward-pointing, like gmeow:wasGeneratedBy, but attaching to the statement rather than to an entity: gmeow:wasGeneratedBy says a thing was produced by an activity, this says a particular assertion was. Deliberately domain-free, since any statement a session emits may be annotated this way and the annotated subjects share no class. Distinct from gmeow:derivedByFunction, which names a pure function a derived observation was computed with, not an audited call event."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:answer gmeow:derivedBy ex:searchCall ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: ATTRIBUTION, never endorsement — the edge records which call an assertion came out of and says nothing about whether that assertion is true, so an answer later refuted keeps this edge rather than losing it. No rdfs:domain is asserted, deliberately: the annotated subjects share no class, so nothing here checks that the subject is a statement rather than a thing, and that discipline belongs to whichever reification the recording harness uses. The range is a gmeow:ToolCall and nothing wider — a whole session, the requesting gmeow:ModelInvocation, and the bare gmeow:SoftwareAgent that was called are all out of scope, because only the call event carries the arguments and the verbatim payload an auditor has to read."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid using it where the subject is an entity the call produced rather than an assertion about one — that is gmeow:wasGeneratedBy — and avoid it for a computation with no call event, which is gmeow:derivedByFunction."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Annotate the result statement with the gmeow:ToolCall it came out of, and let the call itself carry the tool, the arguments, and the verbatim payload; a reader recovers the whole provenance chain by following this one edge back."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when an assertion an agent emits must remain traceable to the specific tool call that yielded it, so a later reader can audit the answer rather than trusting it."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:sessionStoreSegment
    a logic:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:ToolCall ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    rdfs:label "session store segment"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    skos:definition "The identifier of the append-only session-store segment this call's audit record was appended to. A session's trajectory is written as an ordered run of segments rather than as one rewritten whole, so naming the segment makes the record locatable without re-reading the entire store, and makes an audit that spans several commits reconstructible in order."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:call gmeow:sessionStoreSegment \"0003\" ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: a LOCATOR, not an ordering and not the payload. It names which segment holds the audit record, never an offset inside that segment, and comparing two identifiers is not a sanctioned way to order two calls — replay order comes from the store's append order and from the call's own gmeow:atTime, never from arithmetic on this literal. Nor is it a filesystem path: it names the store's own segment identity, so relocating or renaming the underlying files leaves the record true. Exactly one value per call (gmeow:sessionStoreSegmentFunctionality) — bytes that landed in two segments are a broken append, not a second value."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid using it to carry the audit payload itself (that is gmeow:toolResult) and avoid re-pointing an existing call at a different segment, which would falsify an append-only record."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Record the segment identifier at the moment the audit bytes are appended, so the identifier and the bytes are committed together and the trajectory can be replayed in append order."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to locate a tool call's audit record inside an append-only session store, when the store is written as a run of segments rather than as one rewritten file."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:toolArguments
    a logic:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:ToolCall ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    rdfs:label "tool arguments"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    skos:definition "The opaque arguments literal recorded for a tool call, or a digest locator explicitly defined by its recording profile. This event payload is not a generated entity link. The generic contentDigest contract does not define prefixed locator strings. At most one value is admitted; structured RDF uses toolArgumentsStructured."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to retain an opaque payload supplied by the recording profile."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid requiring an opaque JSON literal when structured RDF is available or inferring a generated artifact from event content."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Keep the source literal and its declared profile. For role-specific media metadata, use the corresponding structured companion with structuredTerm, mediaType and charset on its payload occurrence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "Opaque arguments and result media are described on separate role-bound payload occurrences."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:toolResult
    a logic:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:ToolCall ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    rdfs:label "tool result"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
    skos:definition "The opaque result literal recorded for a tool call, or a digest locator explicitly defined by its recording profile. This event payload is not a generated entity link. The generic contentDigest contract does not define prefixed locator strings. At most one value is admitted; structured RDF uses toolResultStructured."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to retain an opaque payload supplied by the recording profile."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid requiring an opaque JSON literal when structured RDF is available or inferring a generated artifact from event content."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Keep the source literal and its declared profile. For role-specific media metadata, use the corresponding structured companion with structuredTerm, mediaType and charset on its payload occurrence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "Opaque arguments and result media are described on separate role-bound payload occurrences."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

gmeow:usedTool
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain gmeow:ToolCall ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    rdfs:label "used tool"@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:range gmeow:SoftwareAgent ;
    skos:definition "The tool that was called — a SoftwareAgent (an MCP tool, a search service, a code runner). Deliberately no Tool subclass: tool-ness is the role the agent plays in this call event, not an identity. Functional: one tool per call; a multi-tool turn is several ToolCalls."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic>
    a logic:Ontology ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow> ;
    rdfs:comment """Agentic tool-call provenance — the ModelInvocation idiom one level down.

DOCTRINE.
  * THE MODELINVOCATION IDIOM, EXACTLY: ToolCall is a gufo:EventType under gmeow:Activity with one functional agent link (usedTool, mirroring usedModel) and verbatim call parameters as datatype properties (mirroring the sampling trio). 'Which tool, called by which invocation, with what arguments, at what time?' is answerable after the fact.
  * NO FORWARD OUTPUT ENTITY PROPERTY (Principle 5): an entity the call produced — a stored claim, a written file, a minted node — links BACK via gmeow:wasGeneratedBy, exactly as claims link back to their ModelInvocation. gmeow:toolResult records the verbatim PAYLOAD of the event itself, never an entity link.
  * PAYLOAD REPRESENTATIONS: toolArguments/toolResult retain opaque literals or locators defined by an explicit recording profile. A prefixed locator string is not the generic contentDigest contract. toolArgumentsStructured/toolResultStructured instead link role-bound StructuredValue occurrences; opaque media metadata belongs on the individual payload occurrence. Coexisting representations do not imply equivalence or conversion.
  * TOOLS ARE SOFTWARE AGENTS — deliberately no Tool subclass: tool-ness is the role the agent plays in this call event, not an identity (roles classify, never reify — the Persona lesson, register/persona design). An MCP tool, a search service, and a code runner are SoftwareAgents that happen to be called.
  * calledByInvocation IS OPTIONAL: a recording harness may not expose the requesting model invocation; a ToolCall without one is still auditable provenance. The result feeds a LATER invocation — that ordering is temporal (atTime), not a TBox link.
  * THIN MEANS THIN (Principle 15): the named consumer is the agentic runtime's tool-call mode; the gmeow memory MCP triad is the first live producer (its store/revise calls record themselves). Growth requires a concrete consumer; structured payload companions serve callers that admit native RDF instead of opaque JSON objects. The T6 read-only trajectory audit is the verification consumer that finally exercises a recorded ToolCall SEQUENCE — but it mints NO aggregate term here: a recorded sequence is audited by treating each call as a logic:ActionSchema instance (logic:instantiatesSchema) anchored on the existing logic: mereology, run through the Transaction-Logic engine. The aggregate's structure lives in the logic: core, not as new agentic vocabulary; the aggregate remains in the grounding kernel (worked example: examples/trajectory-audit.ttl).
  * ALIGNMENTS: ToolCall is prov:Activity by inheritance (the provenance set). OpenAI function-calling, Anthropic tool_use, and MCP tool schemas are JSON specs with no stable RDF namespace — bridging is a projection concern (the Workflow Run Crate worked example and the OpenLineage precedent), recorded in the mapping trailer."""@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    rdfs:label "GMEOW Agentic Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The GMEOW Agentic Module — tool-call provenance: an agent's ACTIONS join the same provenance graph as its claims. DELIBERATELY THIN."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxConfigBox ,
        gmeow:boxTBox .

# =========================================================================== #
# Declarative constraint axioms — the closed-
# world cardinality / class / literal obligations the hand-authored
# gmeow:ToolCallShape states, authored here once as logic:Restriction axioms and
# PROJECTED to generated/shapes/validation-shapes.ttl by derive_validation_shapes
# (Principle 17). logic:maxQualifiedCardinality (logic:onClass logic:Thing) -> sh:maxCount;
# logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 (logic:onClass logic:Thing) -> sh:minCount 1 + sh:maxCount 1;
# logic:allValuesFrom C -> sh:class C;
# logic:allValuesFrom rdfs:Literal -> sh:nodeKind sh:Literal (the verbatim payload
# facet). The `sh:nodeKind sh:IRI` facet on the object-valued paths has no
# ordinary-OWL antecedent (logic:Thing lowers to sh:BlankNodeOrIRI, not sh:IRI) and
# stays on the procedural constraint fragment.
# =========================================================================== #

gmeow:ToolCall logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:calledByInvocation ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass logic:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:usedTool ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass logic:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:toolArguments ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange rdfs:Literal ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:toolResult ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onDataRange rdfs:Literal ] .

# exact-one minCount restoration: min-qualified sibling restrictions
# restoring sh:minCount for the reasoner-safe max-qualified exact-one antecedents.
# logic:onClass logic:Thing (not the specific class) so the qualified count degrades to
# the bare sh:minCount/maxCount gmeow:ToolCallShape wants, matching the class
# component already supplied by the someValuesFrom/allValuesFrom restrictions
# in this class's own definition above.
gmeow:ToolCall logic:subClassOf [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:usedTool ; logic:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass logic:Thing ] .

# --- Shape-migration grounding (projected to generated/shapes/validation-shapes.ttl) ---
# gmeow:ToolCallShape: gmeow:calledByInvocation is already OWL FunctionalProperty
# with rdfs:range gmeow:ModelInvocation (sh:maxCount 1); the explicit allValuesFrom
# restriction below is the class-restriction idiom (Pattern 2) alongside it.
gmeow:ToolCall logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:calledByInvocation ; logic:allValuesFrom gmeow:ModelInvocation ] .

# ── logic: assertion carriers for this slice's own terms ────────────────────────
# The canonical logic: carriers for the characteristics and integrity conditions of the
# terms THIS slice owns. Each record names one of this slice's own properties or classes
# through a logic: RBox predicate; the native coherence gate joins the record to enforce
# the condition, and the OWL grounding view projects OWL FunctionalProperty (and friends)
# from it. Authored here rather than in the logic slice because the fact asserted is a
# fact about this slice's own term, and a grounding slice never depends on a non-grounding
# slice (docs/GROUNDING.md, the tier rule): the logic: assertion vocabulary is CONSUMED
# here (gmeow:sliceDependsOn logic), never owned.
#   logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion — logic:characterizes names the property, logic:characteristicSort its characteristic.

gmeow:calledByInvocationFunctionality
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    rdfs:label "calledByInvocation is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:calledByInvocation is functional: a tool call is requested by at most one model invocation, the single requesting invocation that issued it (optional, because a recording harness may not expose it, but never plural)."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:calledByInvocation ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:calledByInvocation ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:calledByInvocation names exactly one value; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:calledByInvocation, logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:calledByInvocation and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:calledByInvocation (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:calledByInvocationFunctionality logic:characterizes gmeow:calledByInvocation ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .
gmeow:sessionStoreSegmentFunctionality
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    rdfs:label "sessionStoreSegment is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:sessionStoreSegment is functional: a tool call's audit record was appended to exactly one append-only session-store segment, the single segment its bytes were committed to. A second value would make the record locatable in two places at once and let a replay re-point an already-committed call at a different segment, which is precisely what an append-only trajectory forbids. This record is not a definition of that term and never a shape: the obligation is reasoned from the record, not restated elsewhere."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:sessionStoreSegment ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:sessionStoreSegment ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:sessionStoreSegment names exactly one value; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:sessionStoreSegment, logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:sessionStoreSegment and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:sessionStoreSegment (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:sessionStoreSegmentFunctionality logic:characterizes gmeow:sessionStoreSegment ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .
gmeow:toolArgumentsFunctionality
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    rdfs:label "toolArguments is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts that toolArguments admits at most one opaque payload literal per tool call. It requires no payload and does not equate the opaque slot with a structured companion."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:toolArguments ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:toolArguments ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to enforce at most one supplied opaque payload without requiring its presence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:toolArguments, logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:toolArguments and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:toolArguments (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:toolArgumentsFunctionality logic:characterizes gmeow:toolArguments ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .
gmeow:toolResultFunctionality
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    rdfs:label "toolResult is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts that toolResult admits at most one opaque payload literal per tool call. It requires no payload and does not equate the opaque slot with a structured companion."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:toolResult ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:toolResult ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to enforce at most one supplied opaque payload without requiring its presence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:toolResult, logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:toolResult and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:toolResult (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:toolResultFunctionality logic:characterizes gmeow:toolResult ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .
gmeow:usedToolFunctionality
    a logic:NamedIndividual ,
        logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    rdfs:label "usedTool is functional"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:usedTool is functional: a tool call invokes exactly one tool, since tool-ness is the role an agent plays in this one call event and a multi-tool turn is recorded as several ToolCalls. This record is not a definition of that term and never a shape: the obligation is reasoned from the record, not restated elsewhere."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:characterizes gmeow:usedTool ;
    logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:usedTool ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the native coherence gate must enforce that gmeow:usedTool names exactly one value; this record is the canonical carrier the gate joins, so the obligation is reasoned rather than restated on a shape surface."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid this record when a second value would make the record ambiguous — retire the assertion instead of weakening it, and never mirror it as a hand-authored shape."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Read together with logic:characteristicSort: the pair (logic:characterizes gmeow:usedTool, logic:characteristicSort logic:functionalProperty) is the whole obligation, and the OWL grounding view projects the matching characteristic from it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Scope: this record carries ONE integrity obligation about gmeow:usedTool and nothing else. It is not a definition of gmeow:usedTool (that lives on the term itself), not a shape, and not a second place to state the term's meaning — retire the record rather than broaden it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:usedToolFunctionality logic:characterizes gmeow:usedTool ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox .

gmeow:AttentionRequest
    a logic:Class, logic:Kind ; logic:subClassOf gmeow:InformationObject ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    rdfs:label "Attention Request"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A recorded request to attend to something, including one raised by a dream report."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:request a gmeow:AttentionRequest ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "The request is an information object; acknowledgement and resolution are separate events."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not collapse acknowledgement, postponement, dismissal and completed attention into one mutable success flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the request, its description and source, and the separate event actors, times, rationale and evidence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when recording the explicit attention-request lifecycle rather than inferring it from silence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:AttentionAcknowledgement
    a logic:Class, logic:Event ; logic:subClassOf gmeow:Activity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    rdfs:label "Attention Acknowledgement"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An event in which an agent acknowledges an attention request without necessarily resolving it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:ack a gmeow:AttentionAcknowledgement ; gmeow:acknowledges ex:request ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Acknowledgement records receipt, not agreement, completion or resolution."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not collapse acknowledgement, postponement, dismissal and completed attention into one mutable success flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the request, its description and source, and the separate event actors, times, rationale and evidence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when recording the explicit attention-request lifecycle rather than inferring it from silence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:AttentionResolution
    a logic:Class, logic:Event ; logic:subClassOf gmeow:Activity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    rdfs:label "Attention Resolution"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An event recording how an agent disposed of an attention request, with rationale and supporting evidence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:resolution a gmeow:AttentionResolution ; gmeow:resolves ex:request ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Addressed, deferred and dismissed are explicit outcomes; none implies deletion of the request."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not collapse acknowledgement, postponement, dismissal and completed attention into one mutable success flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the request, its description and source, and the separate event actors, times, rationale and evidence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when recording the explicit attention-request lifecycle rather than inferring it from silence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:acknowledges
    a logic:ObjectProperty ; logic:domain gmeow:AttentionAcknowledgement ; logic:range gmeow:AttentionRequest ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "acknowledges"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an attention acknowledgement event to the request it acknowledges."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:ack gmeow:acknowledges ex:request ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Multiple acknowledgements may coexist with their own actors and times."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not collapse acknowledgement, postponement, dismissal and completed attention into one mutable success flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the request, its description and source, and the separate event actors, times, rationale and evidence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when recording the explicit attention-request lifecycle rather than inferring it from silence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:resolves
    a logic:ObjectProperty ; logic:domain gmeow:AttentionResolution ; logic:range gmeow:AttentionRequest ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "resolves"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an attention resolution event to the request whose disposition it records."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:resolution gmeow:resolves ex:request ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Resolution does not imply that the requested work succeeded; inspect resolutionOutcome."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not collapse acknowledgement, postponement, dismissal and completed attention into one mutable success flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the request, its description and source, and the separate event actors, times, rationale and evidence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when recording the explicit attention-request lifecycle rather than inferring it from silence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:ResolutionOutcome
    a logic:Class, logic:AbstractIndividualType ; logic:subClassOf logic:QualityValue ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    rdfs:label "Resolution Outcome"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An attributed disposition value for an attention resolution event."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "gmeow:resolutionAddressed a gmeow:ResolutionOutcome ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "An open value vocabulary, distinct from a logical evaluation verdict or task execution status."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not collapse acknowledgement, postponement, dismissal and completed attention into one mutable success flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Use the value with resolutionOutcome on an attributed AttentionResolution event."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when recording the explicit attention-request lifecycle rather than inferring it from silence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:resolutionAddressed
    a gmeow:ResolutionOutcome ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    rdfs:label "addressed"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The resolving agent records that the requested attention was given."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:resolution gmeow:resolutionOutcome gmeow:resolutionAddressed ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "This is the agent’s disposition, not proof that every underlying problem was solved."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not collapse acknowledgement, postponement, dismissal and completed attention into one mutable success flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Use the value with resolutionOutcome on an attributed AttentionResolution event."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when recording the explicit attention-request lifecycle rather than inferring it from silence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:resolutionDeferred
    a gmeow:ResolutionOutcome ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    rdfs:label "deferred"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The resolving agent deliberately postpones the requested attention."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:resolution gmeow:resolutionOutcome gmeow:resolutionDeferred ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "An explicit postponement differs from an unacknowledged or missing record."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not collapse acknowledgement, postponement, dismissal and completed attention into one mutable success flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Use the value with resolutionOutcome on an attributed AttentionResolution event."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when recording the explicit attention-request lifecycle rather than inferring it from silence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:resolutionDismissed
    a gmeow:ResolutionOutcome ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    rdfs:label "dismissed"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The resolving agent deliberately declines the requested attention."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:resolution gmeow:resolutionOutcome gmeow:resolutionDismissed ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Retain the rationale and request; dismissal is not erasure or an inference from silence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not collapse acknowledgement, postponement, dismissal and completed attention into one mutable success flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Use the value with resolutionOutcome on an attributed AttentionResolution event."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when recording the explicit attention-request lifecycle rather than inferring it from silence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:resolutionOutcome
    a logic:ObjectProperty ; logic:domain gmeow:AttentionResolution ; logic:range gmeow:ResolutionOutcome ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "resolution outcome"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an attention resolution event to its recorded disposition."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:resolution gmeow:resolutionOutcome gmeow:resolutionDeferred ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "The outcome belongs to the event; later decisions are new events, not overwritten request states."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not collapse acknowledgement, postponement, dismissal and completed attention into one mutable success flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the request, its description and source, and the separate event actors, times, rationale and evidence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when recording the explicit attention-request lifecycle rather than inferring it from silence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:resolutionRationale
    a logic:DatatypeProperty ; logic:domain gmeow:AttentionResolution ; logic:range rdfs:Literal ;
    logic:subPropertyOf gmeow:statedRationale ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "resolution rationale"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The resolving agent’s stated reason for an attention request disposition."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:resolution gmeow:resolutionRationale \"Return after the visit.\"@en ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Specializes statedRationale while retaining the AttentionResolution domain. Source wording keeps language and direction; the inferred general rationale is not a new source assertion or an independently verified cause."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not collapse acknowledgement, postponement, dismissal and completed attention into one mutable success flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the request, its description and source, and the separate event actors, times, rationale and evidence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when recording the explicit attention-request lifecycle rather than inferring it from silence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:resolutionEvidence
    a logic:ObjectProperty ; logic:domain gmeow:AttentionResolution ; logic:range gmeow:Entity ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "resolution evidence"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an attention resolution to a record or entity offered as evidence for its disposition."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:resolution gmeow:resolutionEvidence ex:receipt ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Evidence is offered by the resolving actor and does not become automatically authoritative."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not collapse acknowledgement, postponement, dismissal and completed attention into one mutable success flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the request, its description and source, and the separate event actors, times, rationale and evidence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when recording the explicit attention-request lifecycle rather than inferring it from silence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:attentionRequestedAt
    a logic:DatatypeProperty ; logic:domain gmeow:AttentionRequest ; logic:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "attention requested at"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The explicitly known instant at which an attention request was raised."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:request gmeow:attentionRequestedAt \"2026-10-10T09:00:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "This is the request time, not the dream’s occurrence time or an acknowledgement or resolution time."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not collapse acknowledgement, postponement, dismissal and completed attention into one mutable success flag."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the request, its description and source, and the separate event actors, times, rationale and evidence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when recording the explicit attention-request lifecycle rather than inferring it from silence."@x-gmeow-english .

# Source-faithful goals, attempts and self-commitments (Principles 4, 9, 17).

gmeow:attentionMessage
    a logic:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "attention message"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The verbatim source message of an AttentionRequest, retaining supplied language and direction. A message neither acknowledges the request nor asserts that its requested work was performed."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the source explicitly supplies this relation and its context."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid inventing missing source bindings or inferring execution and success from this record alone."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain actual source values, identities and attribution; preserve supplied wording, language and direction."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Source evidence and configuration remain distinct. Competing attributed records may coexist without a preferred claim."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "ex:record gmeow:attentionMessage \"source-value\" ."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:domain gmeow:AttentionRequest ;
    logic:range rdfs:Literal .

gmeow:AttentionRequest logic:subClassOf [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:attentionMessage ; logic:allValuesFrom [ a rdfs:Datatype ; logic:unionOf ( xsd:string rdf:langString rdf:dirLangString ) ] ] .

# Structured event payloads, authored in the canonical grounding kernel.

gmeow:toolArgumentsStructured
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "tool arguments structured"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The optional single StructuredValue occurrence describing the tool call's arguments payload. It describes event content, not a generated entity; absence asserts neither null nor an empty container."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the arguments payload needs a sanctioned structured RDF home or role-specific media metadata."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid treating this payload description as a generated-output link or inferring equivalence with an opaque literal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Link one payload occurrence; retain its native terms and structure. For opaque media, put the literal in structuredTerm and mediaType and charset on that occurrence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "The arguments payload can be an empty map, explicit null or a native directional literal without a JSON object literal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:domain gmeow:ToolCall ; logic:range gmeow:StructuredValue .

gmeow:toolResultStructured
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "tool result structured"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The optional single StructuredValue occurrence describing the tool call's result payload. It describes event content, not a generated entity; absence asserts neither null nor an empty container."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use when the result payload needs a sanctioned structured RDF home or role-specific media metadata."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Avoid treating this payload description as a generated-output link or inferring equivalence with an opaque literal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Link one payload occurrence; retain its native terms and structure. For opaque media, put the literal in structuredTerm and mediaType and charset on that occurrence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "The result payload can be an empty map, explicit null or a native directional literal without a JSON object literal."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:domain gmeow:ToolCall ; logic:range gmeow:StructuredValue .

gmeow:ToolCall logic:subClassOf
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:toolArgumentsStructured ; logic:allValuesFrom gmeow:StructuredValue ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:toolArgumentsStructured ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass logic:Thing ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:toolResultStructured ; logic:allValuesFrom gmeow:StructuredValue ] ,
    [ a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty gmeow:toolResultStructured ; logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass logic:Thing ] .

# Behavioral drive declarations and explicit program-query source contracts.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .

gmeow:DriveDefinition
    a logic:Class , logic:SubKind ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    rdfs:label "drive definition"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An information specification of a behavioral drive, with an actual history-accumulation program, relieving activity descriptions, a circadian expression, a mode-selection program and declared result dimensions."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "The specification does not assert a physiological state, an evaluated level or a performed call."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "A supplied sleep-pressure definition retains its own actual accumulation and mode clauses."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to publish all four components of an actual drive specification together."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not infer a default scale, initial zero, thresholds or executable consumer from the name."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Supply the actual component resources and dimensions; retain their source and context."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:subClassOf gmeow:InformationObject .

gmeow:DriveStage
    a logic:Class , logic:AbstractIndividualType ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    rdfs:label "drive stage"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An open named quality value used as a stage input or result for a behavioral drive. Actual stageOfDrive memberships identify the definitions in which it is admitted."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Multiple legitimate definition memberships coexist; each selected invocation requires its exact positive membership."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "A named stage may be admitted by two actual drive definitions without equating those definitions."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for an explicitly named stage in an actual drive rule."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not infer severity, order or numeric boundaries from a stage label."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the stage identity and assert each actual stageOfDrive membership."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .

gmeow:CallMode
    a logic:Class , logic:AbstractIndividualType ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    rdfs:label "call mode"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "An open named quality value returned by an activity call-mode selection program."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "A named result does not assert a performed call, transition or globally current mode."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "A source rule returns its actual named brief-response mode for one admitted input tuple."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for the actual named output of a declared mode mapping."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not substitute ontological logic:Mode, interruptibility or task status."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Preserve the supplied mode identity and the program that derives it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .

gmeow:stageOfDrive
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "stage of drive"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a DriveStage to an actual DriveDefinition admitting it. The relation is nonfunctional; a selected invocation requires the membership in its exact selected definition."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Other actual memberships remain valid and are not universally equated."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "One stage has an explicit membership in each of two source definitions."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to state an actual stage-definition membership."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not infer membership from matching labels or globally cap the stage to one definition."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Link the actual stage and definition; check this exact positive link when selecting inputs."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:domain gmeow:DriveStage ;
    logic:range gmeow:DriveDefinition .

gmeow:driveAccumulationProgram
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "drive accumulation program"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Links a DriveDefinition to its one actual ReasoningProgram for deriving a level and stage from the supplied history, evaluation instant and circadian quantity."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Actual clauses specify history, relief and circadian combination; the link supplies no execution or arithmetic default."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "The linked program queries driveAccumulationResult with two distinct output variables."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for the actual formal accumulation body of a complete drive definition."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not attach a rule name, integrity constraint or empty program as a substitute."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Supply actual clauses, query and evaluation mode; preserve all selected inputs."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:domain gmeow:DriveDefinition ;
    logic:range logic:ReasoningProgram .

gmeow:relievingActivityDescription
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "relieving activity description"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates a DriveDefinition to an actual EventDescription of an activity declared to relieve that drive."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "The description is not a historical Event. Relief amount, timing and matching are supplied by the actual accumulation clauses."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "An actual rest-activity description is declared to relieve one supplied drive."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for each actual relieving activity specification."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not assert that the activity occurred or infer reset, subtraction or permission."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Link the actual EventDescription and retain the rule’s explicit relief semantics."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:domain gmeow:DriveDefinition ;
    logic:range gmeow:EventDescription .

gmeow:driveCircadianExpression
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "drive circadian expression"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Links a DriveDefinition to its one actual concrete mathematical expression AST for its circadian term."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Actual symbols, bindings, operators and quantities remain required; no period, phase or amplitude is inferred."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "A supplied expression retains its actual time input and explicitly authored parameters."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for the structured circadian expression of a complete drive specification."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not substitute a formula string or infer a daily cosine or supported evaluator."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Supply the actual AST and bind each selected external symbol to its actual Quantity."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:domain gmeow:DriveDefinition ;
    logic:range math:MathematicalExpression .

gmeow:driveModeProgram
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "drive mode program"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Links a DriveDefinition to its one actual ReasoningProgram mapping definition, activity description, drive stage and supplied draw to a named CallMode."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "The same actual program declares the drive’s call-mode effect and selection. A constant-output branch remains valid."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "The actual query uses activityCallModeResult and retains the supplied draw unchanged."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use for an actual data-authored activity, stage and draw mapping."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not drop an input, choose a first row, invent a default mode or imply PRNG execution."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Publish actual clauses and query; require one named result for each completed selected invocation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:domain gmeow:DriveDefinition ;
    logic:range logic:ReasoningProgram .

gmeow:driveLevelDimension
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "drive level dimension"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Links a DriveDefinition to the one actual mathematical Dimension required of its level result Quantity."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Declaring a dimension supplies neither a magnitude, unit, scale nor evaluated result."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "An actual level Quantity retains the dimension explicitly selected by its definition."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to declare the actual dimensional contract of a drive level."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not infer dimensionless pressure or convert an original duration into a numeric level."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Link the supplied Math Dimension and check the actual returned Quantity against it."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:domain gmeow:DriveDefinition ;
    logic:range math:Dimension .

gmeow:driveCircadianDimension
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "drive circadian dimension"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Links a DriveDefinition to the one actual mathematical Dimension required of its circadian result Quantity."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "This dimension need not equal the level dimension; their combination requires actual formal clauses."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "A supplied circadian Quantity carries its definition’s actual declared dimension."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to state the actual output dimension of the selected circadian expression."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not infer a dimensionless default or direct addition to the accumulated level."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the actual Dimension and require its positive link on a selected result Quantity."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:domain gmeow:DriveDefinition ;
    logic:range math:Dimension .

gmeow:driveHistoryClause
    a logic:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxRBox ;
    rdfs:label "drive history clause"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Relates an actual InformationObject history-source record to a selected Formula fact used as drive-history input."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "The relation is nonfunctional. Actual source identities and supplied order or multiplicity facts are retained without asserting completeness."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "An unordered history source selects its actual event facts without synthesizing a sequence."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to identify actual selected history facts for an accumulation invocation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not invent events, total order, duplicate occurrences, a snapshot or complete-history claims."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Link actual atomic Formula trees; preserve source records and only their supplied ordering and repetition."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:domain gmeow:InformationObject ;
    logic:range logic:Formula .

gmeow:driveCircadianInput
    a logic:Type , logic:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    rdfs:label "drive circadian input relation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The reified four-place relation (definition, evaluation instant, mathematical symbol, quantity) binding an actual selected expression symbol to its supplied Quantity."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "Bindings are scoped by the actual definition and evaluation instant. The relation is a Formula symbol, not a binary RDF property or input-injection API."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "One actual symbol is bound to its supplied time Quantity at the actual evaluation instant."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as logic:relation on an actual four-argument Formula atom."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not infer a clock coordinate, unit, phase or default binding from the symbol’s name."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Supply four indexed TermCarriers and preserve the actual symbol identity and Quantity."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:driveCircadianResult
    a logic:Type , logic:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    rdfs:label "drive circadian result relation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The reified three-place relation (definition, evaluation instant, circadian quantity) identifying the actual selected expression result."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "An asserted result atom alone does not prove expression evaluation or dimensional correctness."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "An evaluated circadian Quantity is associated with the same definition and supplied instant."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as logic:relation on the actual three-argument result atom."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not certify an arbitrary supplied quantity as an evaluated result."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Retain the exact definition, instant, Quantity and actual evaluation evidence."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:driveAccumulationResult
    a logic:Type , logic:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    rdfs:label "drive accumulation result relation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The reified six-place relation (definition, history, evaluation instant, circadian quantity, level quantity, stage) fixing accumulation inputs and its two output roles."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "The first four positions are inputs; the last two are distinct query variables. Actual execution must return one admitted level-stage pair."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "An actual accumulation query binds its level and stage through the authored clauses."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as the actual accumulation program’s query relation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not infer arithmetic, stage thresholds, source completeness or completed evaluation from the signature."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Supply six indexed arguments and actual clauses; check result dimensions and the selected stage membership."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:activityCallModeResult
    a logic:Type , logic:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxABox ;
    rdfs:label "activity call-mode result relation"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The reified five-place relation (definition, activity description, stage, draw, mode) fixing the four inputs and named CallMode output of mode selection."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "The draw retains its original supported RDF term. Constant-mode branches are valid; input preservation remains mandatory."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "A completed admitted input tuple derives exactly one named mode from actual clauses."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use as the actual mode program’s query relation."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not infer randomness, draw generation, output variation or a performed activity."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Supply five indexed arguments, bind the exact selected inputs and return the actual named mode."@x-gmeow-english .

gmeow:DriveProgramQueryConstraint
    a logic:Constraint ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agentic> ;
    gmeow:graphBoxRole gmeow:boxTBox ;
    rdfs:label "drive program query constraint"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Requires each linked drive program query to use its exact result relation, required argument positions, admitted input carrier roles and distinct output-variable names; a definition input is a template variable or the exact selected definition IRI."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:scopeNote "The law checks actual Formula and TermCarrier metadata; it supplies no caller-input injection executor."@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:example "A mode query missing its draw argument violates the required-position law."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:useWhen "Use to reject malformed selected drive query declarations."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:avoidWhen "Do not treat a signature label as arity validation or a valid declaration as completed execution."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:howToUse "Validate actual query relations and indexed carriers under the selected DriveDefinition."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:formalizes gmeow:DriveDefinition ;
    logic:message "Requires each linked drive program query to use its exact result relation, required argument positions, admitted input carrier roles and distinct output-variable names; a definition input is a template variable or the exact selected definition IRI."@x-gmeow-english ;
    logic:integrity _:driveDriveProgramQueryConstraint1 .

